.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt ATA 4
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ata
.Nd polled ATA disk driver for the primary IDE channel
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver in the kernel drives one ATA disk: the master of the primary IDE
channel (I/O ports 0x1f0 to 0x1f7 and 0x3f6), with 28-bit LBA addressing
and PIO transfers of one 512-byte sector per command.
At boot it identifies the disk
.Pq Dv IDENTIFY DEVICE
and takes its size from the identify data; a missing drive, an ATAPI or
SATA signature, or a disk larger than 2^28 sectors (128 GiB) is not used.
.Pp
Each read or write waits for the drive's status, polling after every timer
tick or IRQ 14, at most 20000 times; a drive that never becomes ready is an
I/O error, never a hang.
A flush is
.Dv FLUSH CACHE
waited to completion.
.Pp
The kernel uses an NVMe namespace when a usable controller is present
.Pq Xr nvme 4 ,
and otherwise this disk.
Above the driver nothing knows which is in use: the block device is a
kernel object whose one read-write handle belongs to the file server
.Pq Xr filesystem 7 .
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
On the console:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql BLOCK DEVICE OK sectors=N
a disk was found, N sectors of 512 bytes.
.It Ql BLOCK BACKEND ata access=read-write
the block device is this disk.
.It Ql block: no device
no usable disk: the boot has no block device.
.It Ql BLOCK DEVICE FAILED: Ar error
the disk failed at boot; the machine stops.
.El
.Sh QUALIFICATION
QEMU-qualified on QEMU's PIIX IDE controller with a raw image attached as
.Ql -drive file=IMAGE,format=raw,if=ide,index=0 :
this is the disk of the operator image
.Pq Xr afterboot 8
and of every SSH, file server, and crash-consistency matrix of the
platform, and of the kernel's durable-boot tests.
Under QEMU a write completes only after QEMU's own
.Fn write
of that sector returned, so an acknowledged sector survives QEMU ending
abruptly, and a flush becomes the host's
.Fn fdatasync .
No claim is made about power loss on real hardware.
.Pp
Physical hardware qualification: none.
The physical boot image refuses every disk write and has not yet been
booted on hardware.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvme 4 ,
.Xr filesystem 7 ,
.Xr afterboot 8
.Sh CAVEATS
PIO, one sector per command, polled: throughput is low by design.
No secondary channel, no slave drive, no DMA, no 48-bit addressing, no
SATA (AHCI) controller.
